Read on 31 October 2026, about 02:45 UTC: Leanpub's store search, the Leanpub market study (03), and a general web search (US-indexed, so not exhaustive). No number here needs to reach the book, so nothing went into claims/. If the study prints one, ask and I will register it.

"Agentic workflows": in use, and crowded.
- Leanpub: "AI Agents & Agentic Workflows in Production", and a Swift book whose description uses the phrase (store search, "agentic workflows").
- Wider market: "The Agentic Workflow" (Silas Redmond, audiobook, 23 January 2026); "Building Agentic AI: Workflows, Fine-Tuning, Optimization, and Deployment" (Sinan Ozdemir, Addison-Wesley, 2026); "Building Agentic AI Workflows" (self-published; listings disagree on the edition).
- The phrase is also how vendors' explainers describe their products (Slack, Airtable, Oracle). Alone it says the category, not this book.
- Leanpub's "Agentic Engineering" category is the crowded slot: 18 pages of results on 30 October (study 03), mostly engineering and coding handbooks.

"Agentic team": no book title found.
- Near it: "The Agentic Organization" (Jonathan Waite, an executive guide to hybrid teams); "Agentic Leadership"; a Coursera course, "Foundations of Agentic Teams".
- Leanpub's search returned nothing relevant for it (its result list for that phrase is unrelated books, so read it as no match).

"Agents that work together": no book title found. Nearest is a Substack essay, "When Agents Work Together".

N1 to N6, exact titles: no clash found for any of the six. "Brakes So We Can Go Faster", "Open Agentic Workflows", "Agentic Workflows, Shown Working" and "The Plumbing of Agentic Teams" return nothing as phrases. "The Agentic Team" and "Agents That Work Together" are covered above.

The slots, as the market reads tonight:
- Crowded: "agentic" plus engineering, coding or AI. The Leanpub category, and most new titles.
- Busy but generic: "agentic workflows". Readers will meet it, so it needs a subtitle that says what only this book has.
- Open: a team of agents as the subject ("agentic team", "agents that work together"), a real project shown in full ("shown working", "open record"), and the operational side (plumbing, brakes). No title I found takes any of these.

Caveats: search engines and Leanpub's search are not complete lists. Before a name is signed, a check of the exact title at Amazon and at the ISBN agency would close the gap. Say if you want it.

